g_date":"2026-06-22","published":"2026-06-15","filename":"mg474-barnstaple-2026-06-22-town-council-meeting-5656-2026-06-22-annual-governance-accountabil.pdf"}],"notes":{"gss":"mg474","schema":2,"council":"Barnstaple Town Council","facts":[{"key":"paper_purpose","value":"pre-application process briefing to F&GP explaining how a town/parish council applies for a Public Works Loan for renovation and improvement works to Town Council properties","as_at":"2026-01-12","source":{"title":"Public Works Loan Borrowings Report (s5079) \u2014 Finance & General Purposes Committee, 12 January 2026","url":"https://BarnstapleTownCouncil.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s5079/2026-01-12-borrowings-report-for-f-gp.pdf","doc_id":5079,"text":"papers/mg474/5079.txt"},"note":"\u00a71.2 (p1): 'to explain the requirements for the application process.' \u00a72.1 recommendation: 'To consider and approve the process of applying for a Public Works Loan to undertake capital works to Town Council properties.' \u00a73.1 reason: renovation costs are 'beyond the current revenue of reserves budgets of the Council.' The decision to apply must be made by Full Town Council (\u00a74.3, \u00a75.2.1), not by F&GP; F&GP is being asked to approve the process only. Application route runs through DALC (Devon Association of Local Councils) and requires MHCLG borrowing approval before drawing (\u00a74.4)."},{"key":"indicative_annuity_quotes_8_jan_2026","value":"quotes on \u00a3800,000: 10y 4.97% \u00a351,245 half-yearly / \u00a31,024,900 total; 15y 5.32% \u00a339,042 / \u00a31,171,265; 20y 5.64% \u00a333,610 / \u00a31,344,404; 25y 5.86% \u00a330,680 / \u00a31,534,020","as_at":"2026-01-08","source":{"title":"Public Works Loan Borrowings Report (s5079)","url":"https://BarnstapleTownCouncil.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s5079/2026-01-12-borrowings-report-for-f-gp.pdf","doc_id":5079,"text":"papers/mg474/5079.txt"},"note":"\u00a74.8.2 (p2) table verbatim. \u00a74.8.1 states the quotes are for a hypothetical \u00a3800,000 loan and 'were received on 8th January 2026'. These are borrower-facing repayment schedules at a specific principal and repayment method, not standard PWLB curve rows, and no drawdown has occurred \u2014 the council is being asked to authorise the application process."},{"key":"indicative_eip_quotes_8_jan_2026","value":"quotes on \u00a3800,000: 10y 4.94% \u00a359,760 initial half-yearly (reducing \u00a3988) / \u00a31,007,480 total; 15y 5.23% \u00a347,587 (reducing \u00a3697) / \u00a31,124,260; 20y 5.50% \u00a342,000 (reducing \u00a3550) / \u00a31,251,000; 25y 5.71% \u00a338,840 (reducing \u00a3457) / \u00a31,382,420","as_at":"2026-01-08","source":{"title":"Public Works Loan Borrowings Report (s5079)","url":"https://BarnstapleTownCouncil.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s5079/2026-01-12-borrowings-report-for-f-gp.pdf","doc_id":5079,"text":"papers/mg474/5079.txt"},"note":"\u00a74.8.3 (p2) table verbatim. Same \u00a3800,000 hypothetical, same 8 January 2026 quote date, EIP method."},{"key":"existing_debt","value":"not stated in the paper; our own PWLB file holds NO loans for Barnstaple Town Council","as_at":"2026-01-12","source":{"title":"OUR file \u2014 price_book.py --find 'Barnstaple' / 'BARNSTAPLE' / 'BARNSTA'","url":"","doc_id":null,"text":"papers/mg474/5079.txt"},"note":"OUR data \u2014 NOT from the paper. All three --find searches return 'no borrower matching'. The paper carries no reference to any existing PWLB debt; the report is framed as a first application. bc-loans DOES include town/parish council borrowers (Ashburton, Axminster, Bideford and Bovey Tracey all sit on the Devon list), so absence for Barnstaple is genuine rather than a filter effect. Consistent with the paper \u2014 nothing to reconcile."},{"key":"cfr_and_balance_sheet_identity","value":"not stated \u2014 town/parish councils sit outside the principal-authority prudential framework and no CFR, external borrowing total, other long-term liabilities or internal borrowing figures appear in the paper","as_at":"2026-01-12","source":{"title":"Public Works Loan Borrowings Report (s5079)","url":"https://BarnstapleTownCouncil.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s5079/2026-01-12-borrowings-report-for-f-gp.pdf","doc_id":5079,"text":"papers/mg474/5079.txt"},"note":"The identity CFR \u2212 external borrowing \u2212 OLTL = internal borrowing cannot be tested from this paper and would not be expected to appear in any town-council paper. Absence recorded, no figure invented."}],"threads":[],"meetings":{"5079-finance-and-general-purposes-committee":{"date":"2026-01-12","committee":"Finance & General Purposes Committee","note":"The meeting at which this report was received. That date has now PASSED (today is 2026-08-15). The decision to apply for a PWL requires Full Town Council resolution (\u00a74.3, \u00a75.2.1) \u2014 no subsequent meeting date is stated in this paper."}},"summary":{"written":"2026-08-15","text":"<p>Barnstaple Town Council's Public Works Loan Borrowings Report is a three-page pre-application process briefing to the Finance & General Purposes Committee on 12 January 2026. Its purpose (\u00a71.2, p1) is to explain the requirements for applying for a Public Works Loan to fund renovation and improvement works to Town Council properties, the costs of which are stated (\u00a73.1) to be beyond the council's current revenue and reserves. It is not a treasury management strategy, not an outturn and not a monitoring report; it carries no CFR, no maturity profile, no MRP policy and no prudential indicators, and none of those would be expected in a town/parish council paper \u2014 the prudential/CIPFA framework the platform is built around is a principal-authority regime.</p><p>The numerical content is confined to two indicative-quote tables at \u00a74.8 (p2), both for a hypothetical \u00a3800,000 loan and dated 8 January 2026. \u00a74.8.2 sets out fixed-rate annuity quotes over 10, 15, 20 and 25 years (4.97%, 5.32%, 5.64%, 5.86%) with half-yearly costs of \u00a351,245, \u00a339,042, \u00a333,610 and \u00a330,680 and total costs from \u00a31,024,900 to \u00a31,534,020. \u00a74.8.3 sets out fixed-rate EIP quotes on the same principal at 4.94%, 5.23%, 5.50% and 5.71% with initial half-yearly costs from \u00a359,760 (reducing \u00a3988) to \u00a338,840 (reducing \u00a3457) and totals from \u00a31,007,480 to \u00a31,382,420. These are quotes for a decision that had not yet been made \u2014 the recommendation is only to approve the process, and the loan itself requires Full Town Council resolution and MHCLG borrowing approval (\u00a74.3, \u00a74.4).</p><p>Our PWLB file holds no loans for Barnstaple Town Council \u2014 searches on 'Barnstaple', 'BARNSTAPLE' and 'BARNSTA' all return no borrower \u2014 which is consistent with the paper. Nearby Devon town councils (Ashburton, Axminster, Bideford, Bovey Tracey) and the principal authority North Devon District Council do appear in bc-loans, so the absence is genuine rather than a filter effect. The balance-sheet identity CFR \u2212 external borrowing \u2212 OLTL = internal borrowing cannot be tested from this paper; absence recorded, no figure invented. No email is drafted from this document: the paper carries no treasury position worth writing to anyone about, the council is not in our target audience (S151 officers of principal authorities), the named officer is the Town Clerk rather than a statutory finance officer, and no email address is printed in the paper.</p>"},"courses":{"scored":false,"read":[],"text_held":true},"contacts":[{"name":"Robert Ward","role":"Town Clerk","email":null,"note":"'Report by' block on the front sheet (p1). Barnstaple Town Council is a parish-tier authority; the Town Clerk is the senior officer but is NOT a statutory Section 151 officer in the principal-authority sense \u2014 town/parish councils sit outside that regime. NO email address printed in the paper \u2014 do not guess."}],"status":{"state":"read-blocked","written_up":true,"contact":false,"as_at":"2026-08-15","source_text_held":true,"note":"Pre-application process briefing from a town (parish-tier) council with no PWLB debt in our file. The paper carries no existing loan book, no CFR, no maturity profile, no MRP policy and no prudential indicators \u2014 and none would be expected, because town/parish councils sit outside the principal-authority prudential regime. The only numerical content is two tables of indicative repayment quotes for a hypothetical \u00a3800,000 first loan, dated 8 January 2026. The balance-sheet identity cannot be tested from this paper (absence recorded, no figure invented). Loan-book reconciliation is empty on both sides: the paper prints no book and our file holds none for this borrower \u2014 confirmed by --find 'Barnstaple', 'BARNSTAPLE' and 'BARNSTA', all returning no borrower, with nearby Devon town councils confirmed present in bc-loans so absence is genuine. No draft written and none should be: outside our target audience (S151 officers of principal authorities), no treasury position to hook from, named officer is the Town Clerk not a statutory finance officer, and no email address is printed in the paper.","drafted_by":"routine","needs_review":false,"state_was":"read-thin"},"emails":{}}}